1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,884
Maya is moving her weather pipeline from IDL to Python.

2
00:00:04,134 --> 00:00:06,630
It has to match the old one. One to one.

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:11,236
She compares them. Every single row differs.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,224
Float precision. A renamed column. A bug she fixed on purpose.

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:21,348
Somewhere in there hides a real bug.

6
00:00:21,598 --> 00:00:24,166
Which differences are fixes, and which are corruption?

7
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,278
Veridelta compares two datasets under rules you declare.

8
00:00:30,528 --> 00:00:32,784
Nothing is forgiven unless a rule says so.

9
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:39,900
Declare the rename. Let Veridelta suggest the rest from your data. Accept the fix with a baseline.

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:47,640
What's left is the real bug. Four readings lost their minus sign, and CI fails the pull request.

11
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,588
Fix it, and it passes. One to one.

12
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:57,288
Porting a pipeline of your own? Start with Veridelta's six tutorials.
